mobile broadband and narrowband services; develops and sells satellite, wireless products, and terminals; and design, develop, and produce space system solutions for geostationary, medium, and low earth orbit. The company also provides in-flight connectivity, narrowband safety operational data, and other complementary services; multimedia connectivity for military and government; tactical and beyond-line-of-sight communications; intelligence surveillance and reconnaissance; L-band advanced communications element terminals; enterprise connectivity solutions; Internet-of-Things; and L-band managed, energy, and prepaid internet services. In addition, it offers networking, cybersecurity, and information assurance products and services; high assurance internet protocol encryption solutions; MOJO expeditionary tactical gateway; government satellite communication systems, mobile and fixed broadband modems, ground and airborne terminals, antennas and gateways, Ka-band earth stations, and other multi-band/multi-function antennas, as well as design products for manpacks, aircraft, unmanned aerial vehicles, seagoing vessels, ground-mobile vehicles, space-based systems, and fixed applications. Further, the company designs and develops GEO, LEO, and MEO satellites, payload, antenna technologies, and other small satellite platforms; develops commercial communication satellite product, orchestration of sovereign and multi-orbit solutions, and direct-to-device; and licenses intellectual property. Viasat, Inc. was incorporated in 1986 and is headquartered in Carlsbad, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark D. Dankberg | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $663K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["ViaSat, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $9.4B market cap on $4.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 34% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"20,088 Viasat Inc. $VSAT Shares Sold by Illinois Municipal Retirement Fund","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/20088-viasat-inc-vsat-shares-sold-by-illinois-municipal-retirement-fund.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794560828.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Viasat (NASDAQ:VSAT) and Allot (NASDAQ:ALLT) Critical Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/viasat-nasdaqvsat-and-allot-nasdaqallt-critical-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794525406.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.876,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Viasat (VSAT) Wins NASA NEXUS Role, Is The Valuation Upside Still There?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-vsat/viasat/news/viasat-vsat-wins-nasa-nexus-role-is-the-valuation-upside-sti","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794382067.609,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.888,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Viasat, Inc. (VSAT) Shares Nearly Double Following Cooperation Agreement with Activist Carronade Capital","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link