edian.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 0.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $103 on average, 51% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 1% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value.","Operating margin is running 5pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 3.6% of revenue on R&D and 1.7% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.1x net debt to EBITDA ($1.7B of cash against $6.4B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 0.3x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.98 in the distress zone.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.41)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 22.0% over 3 years, 15.5% over 5 years and 11.5% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.11 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 88% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 26%.","Capex runs 2.6x depreciation (42.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.8%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (11 sales, net $4.8M sold).","The share count has grown 14.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 11.2% of the float, 5.7 days to cover."],"people":["With about 7,000 employees, each generates about $663K of revenue, 1.8x the Technology median, and revenue has grown 11.6% a year across its filed history.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $3.9M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $12K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons"